<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ingria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ingria is a historical region on the southern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a>, around present-day St Petersburg. It was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the seventeenth century. It was lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> and ceded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Peace of Nystad</a> in 1721, part of the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ingria.jpg" alt="Ingria" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oakmanner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ingria_in_Saint_Petersburg_and_its_surrounding_region.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
